---
import StandardPageLayout from "../../layouts/StandardPageLayout.astro";
import Glossary from "../../components/Glossary.astro";
import PageToc from "../../components/PageToc.astro";
import "../../styles/standards-poster.css";
import "../../styles/extended.css";
import HistoryTimeline from "../../components/HistoryTimeline.astro";
import history from "../../data/history.json";
import metadata from "../../data/standards/asbe/asbe38.json";
---

<StandardPageLayout
  code={metadata.code}
  standardType={metadata.framework}
  title={metadata.title}
  description={metadata.description}
  issued={metadata.issued}
  latestAmendment={metadata.latestAmendment}
  status={metadata.status}
  summary={metadata.summary}
  bannerNotice={metadata.bannerNotice}
>
  <Fragment slot="toc">
    <PageToc
      items={[
        { id: "s1", label: "1. Conceptual Framework Linkage" },
        { id: "s2", label: "2. Scope — the 2006 Transition, and Ongoing New Adopters" },
        { id: "s3", label: "3. The General Principle — Retrospective Application, With Exceptions" },
        { id: "s4", label: "4. Mandatory Exceptions to Retrospective Application" },
        { id: "s5", label: "5. Optional Exemptions" },
        { id: "s6", label: "6. The Opening Balance Sheet" },
        { id: "s7", label: "7. Reconciliations Required on Transition" },
        { id: "s8", label: "8. Worked Example — Adjusting Retained Earnings on Transition" },
        { id: "s9", label: "9. Worked Example — Applying a Business Combination Exemption" },
        { id: "s10", label: "10. Disclosure Requirements" },
        { id: "s11", label: "11. Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates" },
        { id: "s12", label: "12. Relationship to IFRS 1" },
        { id: "s13", label: "13. Statement Mapping" },
        { id: "s14", label: "14. Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "15. Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">
<div class="hub-sub">Extended reference poster · Chinese GAAP (ASBE / CAS) · 企业会计准则的首次执行 · China's own "first-time adoption" standard, conceptually parallel to IFRS 1 · RMB examples</div></div></div>



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">China's own dedicated "first-time adoption" standard</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 38 governs HOW an ENTERPRISE prepares ITS OPENING Balance SHEET and TRANSITIONS to the ASBE FRAMEWORK for the FIRST time — a ROLE CONCEPTUALLY paralleling IFRS 1 (FIRST-time Adoption of INTERNATIONAL Financial REPORTING Standards) internationally, THOUGH originally FRAMED around China'S OWN 2006 nationwide TRANSITION to the OVERHAULED ASBE FRAMEWORK.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the 2006 Transition, and Ongoing New Adopters</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Both the historic nationwide rollout and later individual adopters</div><div class="principle">This Standard ORIGINALLY addressed the NATIONWIDE transition of Chinese ENTERPRISES to the OVERHAULED 2006 ASBE FRAMEWORK, but ALSO continues to APPLY to any INDIVIDUAL enterprise ADOPTING ASBE for the FIRST time SUBSEQUENTLY (e.g. a COMPANY previously applying a SIMPLIFIED framework, such as the ACCOUNTING Standards for SMALL Business ENTERPRISES, transitioning UP to full ASBE).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>The General Principle — Retrospective Application, With Exceptions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">As if ASBE had always been applied, subject to specific relief</div><div class="text-supporting">AS a GENERAL principle, an ENTERPRISE APPLIES the ASBE FRAMEWORK RETROSPECTIVELY in ITS opening BALANCE sheet, AS IF ASBE had ALWAYS been APPLIED — SUBJECT to SPECIFIC mandatory EXCEPTIONS and OPTIONAL exemptions (Sections 4 and 5) RECOGNISING that FULL retrospective APPLICATION would, in CERTAIN areas, be EITHER impracticable OR disproportionately COSTLY.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Mandatory Exceptions to Retrospective Application</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Areas where retrospective application is prohibited</div><div class="text-supporting">CERTAIN areas are SPECIFICALLY EXCLUDED from retrospective APPLICATION — MOST notably, PRIOR DERECOGNITION decisions for FINANCIAL assets and LIABILITIES are GENERALLY NOT reopened, and HEDGE accounting RELATIONSHIPS are NOT retrospectively DESIGNATED — REFLECTING that REVISITING such HISTORICAL determinations WITH the BENEFIT of hindsight WOULD undermine the RELIABILITY of the TRANSITION exercise.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Optional Exemptions</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Practical relief an enterprise may elect to apply</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise MAY ELECT certain PRACTICAL exemptions — MOST notably, NOT restating PAST business COMBINATIONS that OCCURRED before the TRANSITION date (RETAINING the PREVIOUS carrying AMOUNTS of goodwill and ACQUIRED assets/LIABILITIES, RATHER than RECALCULATING them under the FULL ASBE No. 20 acquisition METHOD) — a PRACTICAL relief RECOGNISING the DISPROPORTIONATE cost of RECONSTRUCTING historical ACQUISITION accounting.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The Opening Balance Sheet</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">The starting point for the new accounting framework</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise PREPARES an OPENING Balance SHEET at the DATE of TRANSITION — RECOGNISING all ASSETS and LIABILITIES ASBE requires, DERECOGNISING those it does NOT permit, RECLASSIFYING items AS necessary, and MEASURING all RECOGNISED assets and LIABILITIES in ACCORDANCE with ASBE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>Reconciliations Required on Transition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Bridging the old framework to the new</div><div class="text-supporting">AN enterprise ADOPTING ASBE for the FIRST time DISCLOSES a RECONCILIATION of ITS equity and PROFIT or loss UNDER the PREVIOUS framework to THOSE same figures UNDER ASBE, HELPING readers UNDERSTAND the FINANCIAL statement IMPACT of the TRANSITION.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Adjusting Retained Earnings on Transition</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising a previously unrecognised deferred tax asset</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Recognising deferred tax for the first time</div><div class="wk-body">A company transitioning to ASBE previously applied a framework with no deferred tax recognition (the old "tax payable method" — see the companion ASBE No. 18 poster). On transition, it identifies a deductible temporary difference giving rise to a RMB 4,000,000 deferred tax asset.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company RECOGNISES the RMB 4,000,000 deferred TAX asset in ITS OPENING Balance SHEET, WITH a CORRESPONDING adjustment INCREASING opening RETAINED earnings by <strong>RMB 4,000,000</strong>.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Applying a Business Combination Exemption</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Retaining previous carrying amounts rather than restating</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: Not restating a pre-transition acquisition</div><div class="wk-body">A company acquired a subsidiary five years before its ASBE transition date, recognising goodwill under its previous framework's own (different) measurement approach.</div><div class="wk-answer">The company ELECTS the business COMBINATION exemption, RETAINING the PREVIOUS carrying AMOUNT of goodwill AS its OPENING ASBE balance, RATHER than RECALCULATING the ACQUISITION under ASBE No. 20's CURRENT acquisition METHOD.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 38 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Reconciliation of equity and profit or loss from the previous framework to ASBE</span><span>Nature of any exemptions elected on transition</span><span>Explanation of material adjustments made to the opening Balance Sheet</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Which optional exemptions to elect on transition</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Estimates used in the opening Balance Sheet must be consistent with estimates made at that date under the previous framework, adjusted only for accounting policy differences</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IFRS 1</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 38 vs IFRS 1</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 38</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IFRS 1</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>General retrospective principle</span><span>YES, with exceptions/exemptions</span><span>YES, with exceptions/exemptions — converged</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Business combination exemption</span><span>Available</span><span>Available — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY conceptually PARALLEL standard, THOUGH originally FRAMED around China'S OWN specific 2006 TRANSITION context RATHER than a GENERIC, ongoing FIRST-time adoption SCENARIO.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every transition adjustment lands</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Opening Balance Sheet adjustment</span><span><span class="badge bs">BS</span> <span class="badge bo">SCOE</span></span><span>Typically adjusted through opening retained earnings</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 20</span><span>Business Combinations — the standard this Standard's optional business combination exemption relates to</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Date of transition</div><div class="glossary-def">The beginning of the earliest period for which an enterprise presents full comparative information under ASBE for the first time.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Opening Balance Sheet</div><div class="glossary-def">The Balance Sheet prepared at the date of transition, forming the starting point for reporting under the new accounting framework.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bo">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  </div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe38 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
